1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,779
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

2
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:06,019
In this lesson, we will configure a department and protect access.

3
00:00:06,489 --> 00:00:10,970
Wrong time zones distort schedules, and broad permissions expose work

4
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:12,600
to people who do not need it.

5
00:00:13,029 --> 00:00:16,340
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:18,299
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:18,889 --> 00:00:22,649
An administrator sets the department time zone, hides modules the

8
00:00:22,649 --> 00:00:26,900
department will not use, requires two-factor sign-in for administrators

9
00:00:27,129 --> 00:00:29,200
and adds a second administrator.

10
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:34,219
Sets the time zone and address everything else uses, and keeps administrative

11
00:00:34,259 --> 00:00:36,120
access limited and recoverable.

12
00:00:36,679 --> 00:00:40,130
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

13
00:00:40,130 --> 00:00:42,350
scenarios, not default settings.

14
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:44,149
Department Settings.

15
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:47,670
Department address, time zone and core settings.

16
00:00:48,159 --> 00:00:53,030
Confirm the address and time zone; dates, maps and schedules depend on them.

17
00:00:53,699 --> 00:00:54,770
Module settings.

18
00:00:55,209 --> 00:00:58,590
Turn optional modules on or off for the department.

19
00:00:59,010 --> 00:01:02,510
Hide modules you will not use so members see a simpler menu.

20
00:01:03,269 --> 00:01:04,040
Permissions.

21
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:07,600
Who can create calls, see personal information and

22
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,520
perform other sensitive actions.

23
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:13,399
Review each permission; some default to every member.

24
00:01:14,089 --> 00:01:15,740
Two-Factor Authentication.

25
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:18,419
Two-factor sign-in for member accounts.

26
00:01:18,819 --> 00:01:21,890
Enroll every administrator in two-factor sign-in.

27
00:01:22,539 --> 00:01:24,490
Security and session policy.

28
00:01:24,909 --> 00:01:28,480
Two-factor requirements, password rules and session limits.

29
00:01:28,860 --> 00:01:32,090
Require two-factor sign-in for administrators and review

30
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:33,729
password and session rules.

31
00:01:34,349 --> 00:01:36,190
Single sign-on and provisioning.

32
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:40,230
Let members sign in through your identity provider, with optional

33
00:01:40,259 --> 00:01:41,839
automatic account provisioning.

34
00:01:42,349 --> 00:01:45,860
Know your department address and time zone, and choose at least two

35
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:47,789
people who will administer Resgrid.

36
00:01:48,509 --> 00:01:49,429
Audit history.

37
00:01:49,820 --> 00:01:52,249
See who changed department settings and when.

38
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:56,329
Know your department address and time zone, and choose at least two

39
00:01:56,329 --> 00:01:58,299
people who will administer Resgrid.

40
00:01:59,039 --> 00:02:00,779
Account sessions and recovery.

41
00:02:01,230 --> 00:02:04,899
Your own sign-in sessions, password and two-factor settings.

42
00:02:05,359 --> 00:02:08,959
Know your department address and time zone, and choose at least two

43
00:02:08,959 --> 00:02:10,949
people who will administer Resgrid.

44
00:02:11,619 --> 00:02:13,159
Setup help and support.

45
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:16,659
Setup Wizard, Setup Report and Admin Assist.

46
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:20,649
Know your department address and time zone, and choose at least two

47
00:02:20,649 --> 00:02:22,630
people who will administer Resgrid.

48
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:27,509
Passkeys add a device-backed sign-in factor and need deliberate naming,

49
00:02:27,679 --> 00:02:29,699
removal, and recovery handling.

50
00:02:30,239 --> 00:02:33,520
Enroll from account security on a compatible demo device.

51
00:02:33,999 --> 00:02:37,259
Name the credential and review the remaining recovery factors.

52
00:02:37,730 --> 00:02:40,739
Confirm an actual sign-in and check the credential list

53
00:02:40,780 --> 00:02:42,259
after a controlled removal.

54
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:45,479
Confirm availability in the demo department before

55
00:02:45,479 --> 00:02:46,929
recording the live workflow.

56
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,310
For the training scenario, work in this order.

57
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:51,419
Step 1.

58
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:54,369
Confirm the department address and time zone.

59
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:55,540
Step 2.

60
00:02:56,070 --> 00:02:59,490
Choose the modules the department will use and review permissions.

61
00:02:59,950 --> 00:03:00,690
Step 3.

62
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:05,939
Enroll two administrators in MFA before reviewing enforcement and recovery.

63
00:03:06,609 --> 00:03:08,129
Now verify the result.

64
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:11,870
Use separate administrator and member accounts to check allowed

65
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:13,870
actions and resource visibility.

66
00:03:14,269 --> 00:03:17,689
Test recovery before enforcing stricter sign-in rules.

67
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:21,679
A common problem to watch for: Hiding a module is not

68
00:03:21,710 --> 00:03:24,049
evidence that API access stops.

69
00:03:24,449 --> 00:03:28,309
MFA enrollment is separate from a tested factor and recovery path.

70
00:03:28,990 --> 00:03:30,560
Your practice task is simple.

71
00:03:30,999 --> 00:03:35,519
Complete Setup Wizard, save on each owning screen, then Verify again.

72
00:03:35,979 --> 00:03:39,190
Keep unknown checks visible and assign follow-up owners.

73
00:03:39,589 --> 00:03:43,370
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

